---
import '../design/design-aids.css';
import SketchSheet from '../design/SketchSheet.astro';
import SketchArrow from '../design/SketchArrow.astro';
interface Props { stage?: 'identity' | 'recovery'; }
const { stage = 'identity' } = Astro.props;
const titleId = `checkout-${stage}-title`;
---
<figure class="design-aid design-figure paper-surface checkout-trace" aria-labelledby={titleId}>
  <span class="plate-number">Illustration · {stage === 'identity' ? 'One checkout, repeated' : 'Recovery while an attempt is pending'}</span>
  {stage === 'identity' ? <>
    <h3 id={titleId}>Follow checkout K14</h3>
    <p>Ada wants two P7 mugs at EUR 20 each. There are three available. The caller keeps <strong>K14</strong> for this purchase, even when it has to ask again.</p>
    <div class="trace-head" aria-hidden="true"><span>Request</span><span>Committed order for K14</span><span>Available mugs</span></div>
    <div class="trace-row">
      <div><h4>Before the first attempt</h4><p>K14 is saved by the caller.</p></div>
      <div class="record empty"><span class="mobile-label">Committed order</span><p>No order yet</p></div>
      <div class="stock"><span class="mobile-label">Available mugs</span><strong>3</strong></div>
    </div>
    <div class="trace-row">
      <div><h4>First attempt commits</h4><p>Proposes O14, reserves two mugs and records their order line.</p></div>
      <SketchSheet tone="teal"><span class="mobile-label">Committed order</span><div class="key-pair"><strong>K14</strong><SketchArrow /><strong>O14</strong></div><p>Two mugs · EUR 20 each</p></SketchSheet>
      <div class="stock"><span class="mobile-label">Available mugs</span><strong>3 → 1</strong><small>Two reserved</small></div>
    </div>
    <div class="trace-row">
      <div><h4>Same request arrives again</h4><p>Proposes O15 with K14. That key already belongs to O14, so <strong>O15 is not inserted</strong>.</p></div>
      <SketchSheet tone="teal"><span class="mobile-label">Committed order</span><div class="key-pair"><strong>K14</strong><SketchArrow /><strong>O14</strong></div><p>Read and return this order</p></SketchSheet>
      <div class="stock"><span class="mobile-label">Available mugs</span><strong>1 → 1</strong><small>No second reservation</small></div>
    </div>
    <figcaption>Each row shows committed state at a different moment, not another stored copy of O14. Until the first attempt commits, its order, operation key, line and stock change are provisional; rollback removes them together. A repeated request must match the saved customer and purchase details before it can reuse the result.</figcaption>
  </> : <>
    <h3 id={titleId}>An empty lookup can still lead back to O14</h3>
    <p>Checkout K14 is Ada’s purchase of two mugs from three available. The first attempt has inserted O14 and reserved those mugs but has not finished. A new connection cannot see that uncommitted order. It finds nothing when it looks up K14.</p>
    <SketchSheet tone="blue"><h4>Repeat the claim using K14</h4><p>The new attempt proposes O15. The unique-key check waits for the first attempt to finish. <strong>It has not reserved stock again.</strong></p></SketchSheet>
    <p class="branch-label">Two possible endings for the first attempt <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></p>
    <div class="recovery-branches">
      <section>
        <h4>If the first attempt commits</h4>
        <SketchSheet tone="teal"><div class="key-pair"><strong>K14</strong><SketchArrow /><strong>O14</strong></div><p>O14 and its two mugs are kept.</p><p>Available stock: <strong>1</strong></p></SketchSheet>
        <div class="next-step"><SketchArrow direction="down" /><p>The repeated claim inserts nothing.</p></div>
        <p>A subsequent Read Committed query sees O14. Check that its details match and return it.</p>
        <p class="branch-result"><strong>Return O14</strong><span>One order for K14 · stock stays 1</span></p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h4>If the first attempt rolls back</h4>
        <SketchSheet tone="amber"><p><strong>No order for K14</strong></p><p>O14 and its reservation are discarded.</p><p>Available stock: <strong>3</strong></p></SketchSheet>
        <div class="next-step"><SketchArrow direction="down" /><p>The repeated claim inserts O15.</p></div>
        <p>Check stock again, reserve two mugs, add the line and commit this attempt.</p>
        <p class="branch-result"><strong>Return O15 after commit</strong><span>One order for K14 · stock becomes 1</span></p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <figcaption>These are alternative histories in PostgreSQL Read Committed, with no other stock changes and a successful recovery attempt. The lookup alone cannot choose between them; claiming the same unique key coordinates with the unfinished transaction. If the database is unavailable or the wait cannot finish, the outcome remains unresolved.</figcaption>
  </>}
</figure>
<style>
  .trace-head,.trace-row { display:grid; grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.3fr) minmax(0,1.2fr) minmax(0,.65fr); gap:1rem; align-items:center; }
  .trace-head { margin-top:1.5rem; font-size:.75rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .trace-row { border-top:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); padding:1rem 0; }
  .trace-row h4 { margin-bottom:.35rem; }
  .trace-row p { font-size:.8125rem; }
  .empty { color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .key-pair { display:flex; align-items:center; justify-content:center; gap:.4rem; font:500 1rem/1.5 var(--font-mono); }
  .key-pair :global(svg) { width:2.4rem; flex-shrink:0; }
  .stock strong { display:block; font:500 1.25rem/1.5 var(--font-mono); white-space:nowrap; }
  .stock small { display:block; margin-top:.3rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .mobile-label { position:absolute; width:1px; height:1px; overflow:hidden; clip-path:inset(50%); white-space:nowrap; }
  .branch-label { margin:1rem 0; text-align:center; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .recovery-branches { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:1.5rem; }
  .recovery-branches section { min-width:0; margin:0; }
  .recovery-branches h4 { margin:.5rem 0 .8rem; }
  .next-step { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:.5rem; }
  .next-step :global(svg) { flex-shrink:0; }
  .branch-result { padding:.6rem 0 .6rem .8rem; border-left:2px solid var(--teal); }
  .branch-result span { display:block; font-size:.8rem; margin-top:.3rem; }
  @media(max-width:600px) {
    .trace-head { display:none; }
    .trace-row { grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr) minmax(0,.65fr); gap:.8rem; }
    .trace-row > :first-child { grid-column:1/-1; }
    .mobile-label { position:static; display:block; width:auto; height:auto; overflow:visible; clip-path:none; white-space:normal; margin-bottom:.5rem; font-size:.7rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
    .recovery-branches { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:1rem; }
    .recovery-branches section + section { border-top:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong); padding-top:1rem; }
  }
</style>
